oir,\" which is trained randomly and remains fixed. The weights of the output layer are then adjusted to learn the task at hand. Training typically involves initializing the reservoir with random weights and then using a teacher signal to adjust the output weights. Reservoirs are trained offline, and the online phase involves only adjusting the output weights to fit the desired output.\n\nSummarizing the arXiv papers:\n1. \"Integer Echo State Networks: Efficient Reservoir Computing for Digital Hardware\" - Discusses the application of ESNs in digital hardware for anomaly detection.\n2. \"Evolutionary Echo State Network: evolving reservoirs in the Fourier space\" - Focuses on evolving ESNs in the Fourier domain for anomaly detection.\n\nBoth papers explore the use of ESNs for anomaly detection but with different approaches.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":773,"prompt_eval_duration":49866000,"total_duration":2699210400}}